From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: apply a localized msstyles' string table values

Purpose: use the fonts that the Japanese Luna theme defines for Japanese.
A localized msstyles keeps per-language values in its string table, as
"NormalBlue@[Rebar]Font=MS UI Gothic, 9" for the colour/size variant whose
ini resource is NORMALBLUE_INI. XP applies them over the ini, but Wine
read only the ini, so the Japanese XP shell got Tahoma 8 and Franklin
Gothic Medium where XP uses MS UI Gothic, and the Start panel was laid out
20 pixels narrower. Read the string table entries of the selected variant
when the theme is parsed, substitute matching ini values (including
[SysMetrics]) and add the ones the ini lacks. For the opted-in external
shell, all 117 TMT_FONT values reported by tests/theme-props.c --fonts for
26 classes now equal the reference XP machine's. The values are read from
the user's local theme file at run time; nothing is copied or changed.

